{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot motion and perception as separate automata: G1 for motion commands, G2 for obstacle sensors. The specification E1 enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative recovery (turns or full scan) before resuming exploration. Recovery states are one-shot and only allow a single turn or scan action. All uncontrollable events are handled deterministically, and the supervisor quickly returns to exploration after recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to keep models modular and compositional.",
    "Specification automaton encodes the exploration policy: random_walk in clear, short move_forward pulses, conservative turn recovery on obstacles, and rapid return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
  "G": [
